# CSM Mission Control — project primer

This is a Next.js 16 (App Router) dashboard for beehiiv's CSM team.
Production: csm-dash.vercel.app. Single repo, no monorepo.

## Stack

- **Next.js 16** App Router, mostly server components.
  Most pages use `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"` because the
  data is per-user and per-refresh. Wrap async data fetches in
  `<Suspense>` with skeleton fallbacks.
- **TypeScript** strict. Path alias `@/` → `src/`.
- **Tailwind v4** with PostCSS plugin. Semantic colors:
  `text-fg`, `text-muted`, `text-subtle`, `bg-surface`, `bg-canvas`,
  `border-border`, `border-border-strong`, `bg-accent` / `text-accent-fg`.
  Prefer these over raw `gray-*` / `slate-*`.
- **Postgres on Neon** as the KV store (single `kv` table:
  `key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value JSONB`). Accessed via `src/lib/kv.ts`.
  When `DATABASE_URL` is absent, falls back to a local JSON file —
  this matters when running scripts/sync.ts locally.
- **NextAuth (beta v5)** session-based auth, Google provider.
  Session is read via `auth()` in server components and API routes.
- **External integrations**:
  - **Metabase** (q10600, q13268, q23101, q24620) via saved-question API
  - **HubSpot CRM** v3 — companies + properties API, OAuth + Private App tokens
  - **Slack** Web API + webhooks (bot token + signing secret)
  - **Gmail** API with send-as aliases

## Top-level layout

```
src/
  app/                        Next.js routes
    api/                      API routes (POST handlers for mutations)
    csm/ am/ settings/        Page routes
  components/                 React components (mix of server + client)
  lib/
    data/                     KV-backed stores + mappers
    integrations/             External-service clients
    customer-helpers.ts       Shared customer-derivation helpers
    types.ts                  Core domain types (Customer, etc.)
    kv.ts                     Postgres/file KV abstraction
scripts/
  sync.ts                     Nightly Metabase → HubSpot enrichment
data/
  snapshot.enc.json           Committed, encrypted customer snapshot
```

## Data flow at a glance

```
Metabase q10600 → metabaseRowToCustomer() → snapshot.enc.json (commit)
                                          → /api/customers (runtime)
                                          → applyOverride(customer, kv)
                                          → UI
```

The mapper (`src/lib/data/metabase-mapper.ts`) is an **allowlist**.
Any field added to `Customer` upstream must also be added here, or it
silently drops. Multiple production bugs have traced back to this.

## Auth + secrets

- `.env.local` holds dev secrets (not committed).
- Vercel env vars hold prod secrets. Don't commit them, don't paste
  them in chat.
- `DATABASE_URL` is the Neon connection string.
- `HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN` is a Private App token (not OAuth) for the
  HubSpot API calls in `scripts/sync.ts`.

## Useful npm scripts

- `npm run dev` — local server at :3000
- `npm run sync` — refresh `data/snapshot.enc.json` from Metabase+HubSpot
- `npm run typecheck` — full TS check (CI runs this)
- `npm run run:at-risk` — manual at-risk evaluator
- `npm run run:deliverability` — manual deliverability snapshot

## Deploys

- Push to `main` → Vercel deploys to production.
- Push to any other branch → Vercel preview URL.
- Don't `git push --force` to `main`.
